## Prerequisites

- Python [[.PythonVersion]] or newer
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for dependency management
[[- if .Docker]]
- Docker, for the [[.DatabaseLabel]] container
[[- end]]

## Setup

```bash
uv sync
[[- if .Docker]]
docker compose up -d db
[[- end]]
cp .env.example .env
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver
```

`.env.example` ships a placeholder `SECRET_KEY` so the project boots immediately.
Replace it before you deploy anything:

```bash
python -c 'from django.core.management.utils import get_random_secret_key as k; print(k())'
```

## Environment

`ENVIRONMENT` is the only switch for `DEBUG`. Set it to `local`, `test`, `staging`
or `production`. Everything that behaves differently in development — the browsable
API, plain-text logging, the browser-reload endpoint — reads that one value.

Configuration is validated at startup[[if .Pydantic]] by `[[.ModuleName]]/conf.py`[[end]].
A missing or malformed variable stops the process with a message naming the field
rather than failing later at the point of use.

