## Deployment

```bash
python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
python manage.py check --deploy
gunicorn [[.ModuleName]].wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:8000
```

Static files are served by WhiteNoise, so no separate web server is required for
them. Copy `.env.production.example` to `.env` on the server and fill it in;
`settings.production` refuses to start with `ENVIRONMENT=local`.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
|------|------------------|
| `[[.ModuleName]]/` | settings, URLs, WSGI/ASGI, health check and error handlers |
[[- if .MultiEnv]]
| `[[.ModuleName]]/settings/` | `base.py`, `local.py`, `production.py`, `test.py` |
[[- end]]
[[- if .AppName]]
| `[[.AppName]]/models.py` | the model, its queryset and its database constraints |
[[- if .REST]]
| `[[.AppName]]/api/` | serializers, viewsets and API URLs |
[[- end]]
| `[[.AppName]]/templates/` | the pages for this app |
[[- end]]
| `templates/` | base layout, home page and error pages |
| `static/` | CSS and JavaScript |

